<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Il Canto degli italiani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">words September <a href="/years/1847">1847</a>; music 24 November <a href="/years/1847">1847</a>; first public performance 10 December <a href="/years/1847">1847</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Goffredo Mameli, a young patriot from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> with republican and Jacobin sympathies, wrote the words in September 1847 (sources give the 8th or the 10th), inspired by the mass mobilisations that would lead to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolutions-of-1848">revolutions of 1848</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-italian-war-of-independence">First Italian War of Independence</a>. On 10 November he sent the text to the Genoese composer Michele Novaro in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a>, who set it to music on 24 November.</p></div>
